  "worked_solution": "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{x+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of $-1\\text{\u00a0}\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$",
